  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Overlap in the wide channel",
  "description": "Play 5 v 5 with keepers and two jokers on about 50 × 45 metres. Mark a ten-metre-wide channel along each touchline. After at least four passes, the team must get forward through an overlap in a channel for a goal to count. Keep the defender in the channel passive to start with.\n\nVariant: 4 v 4 inside the pitch with four extra players for the attacking team – a winger in each channel and two wall players on the byline beside the goal, with one touch. Whoever passes out to the winger may follow out and make it 2 v 1. Restart from your own keeper after a goal or when the ball goes out. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The ball carrier drives diagonally inside to open up space down the line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The overlapping player calls and speeds up at the right moment."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass diagonally forward into the run once the defender has picked you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Get bodies in the box – the cross needs someone to find."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
